-- AFTER A SCHEMA CHANGE (read this first)
--   Dropping and recreating GOV_SCOPE (or any GOV_* view) also drops the grants on it. After "manage.py governed_views
--   install" has upgraded the objects (for example when the WORKING column was added to GOV_SCOPE), the administrator
--   must run this script again, as SYSDBA, or the governed login loses its rights. This file is not run by the install.
--
-- Grants for the read-only Firebird login that runs governed SQL for the assistant (app/hr_sql).
-- Generated by hand. Nothing in this file is a password. The password is set on the server, never here.
--
-- WHO RUNS THIS, AND WHEN
--   The database administrator, once, as SYSDBA, after "manage.py governed_views install" has created GOV_SCOPE and the
--   GOV_* views. Run it against the database file (for example with isql, connected as SYSDBA).
--
-- HOW TO CREATE THE USER (do this first, on the server, as an administrator)
--   Create a login named MACS_GOV_RT with a password chosen for this purpose, using the server's own tools (gsec, or
--   isql connected as SYSDBA with CREATE USER). The password is not written here, in the repository or in chat. Put
--   the user name in FIREBIRD_GOVERNED_USER and the password in FIREBIRD_GOVERNED_PASSWORD for the runtime process only.
--   If another name is wanted, change it here and in the environment variable.
--
-- WHAT IS GRANTED
--   1. SELECT on the six governed views: GOV_EMPLOYEES, GOV_CHILDREN, GOV_LEAVE, GOV_ORDERS, GOV_SALARY and
--      GOV_LOANS. Firebird 3 runs a view with the rights of the view's owner (the administrator who installed
--      it), so this login needs no right on the MACS or IHR_ tables behind them.
--   2. SELECT, INSERT, DELETE on the scope table GOV_SCOPE. The host fills it per query and it empties at each commit.
--
-- WHAT IS NEVER GRANTED
--   Any right on an IHR_ or MACS table, UPDATE, ALTER, DROP, CREATE, REFERENCES, EXECUTE, and any right to create or
--   change users. The login cannot change the scope rules or the views.
--
-- Not tested on a real database yet: the test suite runs governed SQL as the default login. Check with this login
-- before the assistant's governed SQL is switched on.

GRANT SELECT ON GOV_EMPLOYEES TO MACS_GOV_RT;
GRANT SELECT ON GOV_CHILDREN TO MACS_GOV_RT;
GRANT SELECT ON GOV_LEAVE TO MACS_GOV_RT;
GRANT SELECT ON GOV_ORDERS TO MACS_GOV_RT;
GRANT SELECT ON GOV_SALARY TO MACS_GOV_RT;
GRANT SELECT ON GOV_LOANS TO MACS_GOV_RT;
GRANT SELECT, INSERT, DELETE ON GOV_SCOPE TO MACS_GOV_RT;

COMMIT;
